u, Fukuoka</a></li><li>2012: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2012/03/27/us-dvdblu-ray-release-for-scorseses-george-harrison-documentary/\">US DVD/Blu-ray release for Scorsese’s George Harrison documentary</a></li><li>1999: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1999/03/27/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-sunrise-musical-theatre-sunrise-6/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Sunrise Musical Theatre, Sunrise</a></li><li>1993: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1993/03/27/paul-mccartney-live-western-springs-stadium-auckland/\">Paul McCartney live: Western Springs Stadium, Auckland</a></li><li>1989: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1989/03/27/recording-act-naturally-ringo-starr/\">Recording: Act Naturally by Ringo Starr</a></li><li>1981: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1981/03/27/uk-single-release-watching-the-wheels-john-lennon/\">UK single release: Watching The Wheels by John Lennon</a></li><li>1979: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1979/03/27/mixing-so-glad-to-see-you-here-wings-2/\">Mixing: So Glad To See You Here by Wings</a></li><li>1978: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1978/03/27/us-album-release-london-town-wings/\">US album release: London Town by Wings</a></li><li>1975: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1975/03/27/mixing-rock-show-love-in-song-treat-her-gently-lonely-old-people-crossroads-wings/\">Mixing: Rock Show, Love In Song, Treat Her Gently/Lonely Old People, Crossroads by Wings</a></li><li>1974: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1974/03/27/john-lennon-moves-into-santa-monica-beach-house/\">John Lennon moves into Santa Monica beach house</a></li><li>1972: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1972/03/27/recording-mary-had-a-little-lamb-wings/\">Recording: Mary Had A Little Lamb by Wings</a></li><li>1970: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1970/03/27/mixing-dig-it/\">Mixing: Dig It</a></li><li>1970: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1970/03/27/uk-album-release-sentimental-journey-ringo-starr/\">UK album release: Sentimental Journey by Ringo Starr</a></li><li>1963: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1963/03/27/live-abc-cinema-northampton/\">The Beatles live: ABC Cinema, Northampton</a></li><li>1961: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1961/03/27/travel-liverpool-to-hamburg-2/\">Travel: Liverpool to Hamburg</a></li></ul><p>Want more? Visit the <a title=\"Day after day: the Beatles' history\" href=\"/history/\">Beatles history section</a>.</p></div><div class=\"gm-map\" style=\"position: relative;height: 390px; width: 100%;\"><iframe data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"about:blank\" name=\"gm-map-1\" allowfullscreen=\"\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/?geo_mashup_content=render-map&amp;map_data_key=c5b0b0bd0322643f481787d81f95e0c4&amp;height=390&amp;width=100%&amp;add_overview_control=false&amp;zoom=16&amp;enable_street_view=false&amp;map_type=G_HYBRID_MAP&amp;name=gm-map-1&amp;object_id=133407&amp;map_content=single\" style=\"position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none; overflow: hidden;\" title=\"Geo Mashup Map\"></iframe></div>",
  "textContent": "Filming for the television special James Paul McCartney continued on 27 March 1973 at Elstree Studios. This day’s sequence was based around an unreleased Paul McCartney song, ‘Gotta Sing, Gotta Dance’. It was commissioned in 1972 by Twiggy for a proposed film musical of the same title, which was never made.The version used in James Paul McCartney was scored by Jack Parnell, the musical director, who conducted his orchestra dna vocal group The Ladybirds.The sequence was filmed in two parts. The first had McCartney at a piano, before giving way to an elaborate dance number. McCartney was filmed alone against a blue screen, and 35 dancers were later composited. McCartney’s dance moves were choreographed by Robert Iscove.Produced by ATV, James Paul McCartney was first broadcast on 16 April 1973 in the USA, and 10 May in the UK. It was released on DVD as part of the super deluxe reissue of in Red Rose Speedway December 2018.\n\n\n\n\n\nPage last updated: 1 December 2025Also on this day...2026: Paul McCartney live: Fonda Theatre, Los Angeles2019: Paul McCartney live: Allianz Parque, São Paulo2019: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Sanparesu, Fukuoka2012: US DVD/Blu-ray release for Scorsese’s George Harrison documentary1999: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Sunrise Musical Theatre, Sunrise1993: Paul McCartney live: Western Springs Stadium, Auckland1989: Recording: Act Naturally by Ringo Starr1981: UK single release: Watching The Wheels by John Lennon1979: Mixing: So Glad To See You Here by Wings1978: US album release: London Town by Wings1975: Mixing: Rock Show, Love In Song, Treat Her Gently/Lonely Old People, Crossroads by Wings1974: John Lennon moves into Santa Monica beach house1972: Recording: Mary Had A Little Lamb by Wings1970: Mixing: Dig It1970: UK album release: Sentimental Journey by Ringo Starr1963: The Beatles live: ABC Cinema, Northampton1961: Travel: Liverpool to HamburgWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
